    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **35 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation with a duplicate (lower-cased) email, responding with 409, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckOwnerEmailUnique.java` \u2014 reads the normalized (already lower-cased by `NormalizeOwnerEmail`) request email from the `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, and throws a checked `DuplicateEmailException` if any existing owner's email matches case-insensitively. Email is optional, so a null/blank email is a no-op.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (mirrors `DuplicateTelephoneException`).\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkEmailUnique` step (transactional) right after `checkTelephoneUnique`, alongside the existing repository-based uniqueness checks.\n\nI placed the check after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` so the comparison uses the canonical lower-cased form on both sides, exactly matching the specification.",
